  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Whist. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: 'Whist is the classic English partnership trick-taking game and ancestor of Bridge. 4 players, 2 teams. 52 cards, 13 each. Last card dealt (to dealer) turned face-up = trump. Eldest hand leads. Follow suit. Each trick over 6 = 1 point. Honours (A-K-Q-J of trump): 3 held = 2pts, 4 held = 4pts. Game to 5 (British) or 7 (American). Rubber = best of 3.',
    objective: 'As a partnership, coordinate card play to win the required tricks.',
    gameplay: 'Two partnerships play a Whist-like trick game. Unlike ordinary Whist, partners may communicate within the permitted table convention and a captain may ask for information and direct play.',
    keyRules: [
      'Four players form two partnerships.',
      'Partner communication is allowed under the game convention.',
      'The game is a simpler, faster Whist variant with anticlockwise play recorded in historical descriptions.',
    ],
